# Line-ending policy. 2026-07-26 audit finding 9.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with git's default `core.autocrlf=true`
# rewrites every text file to CRLF. `hooks/repo-integrity.mjs` then failed to
# read the frontmatter block of EVERY agent and skill, reporting all 38 roles
# and all 35 skills as malformed. Pinning LF here stops that happening to this
# repository; the readers in hooks/ are ALSO being made line-ending tolerant,
# because they parse the user's own project files too, and those may legitimately
# be CRLF on Windows. Both halves are needed — this file is not a substitute for
# tolerant parsing.
#
# The CI job that deliberately builds a CRLF working tree overrides this after
# checkout, so the guard itself stays tested.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary — never touch the bytes.
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.vsix  binary

# Text, but pin the ones that break loudly if they arrive as CRLF.
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.svg  text eol=lf
